# NOITE's flying saucer (4fsacaet) starts the real INV, which loses: 0x40a
# lost with -2000 (a negative score lowers NOITE's), the Martian's scene
# (4fmarte), then a life less and back to the bar (4fbar).
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 4fsacaet --ms 46000 --input tools/play/inv-4fsacaet-lose.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 4fsacaet --ms 46000 --fix all,-inv_arcade_rules,-inv_clean_render,-inv_controls_screen --input tools/play/inv-4fsacaet-lose.input
# (The --fix all run pins the Corrigida's arcade INV off, `inv_arcade_rules`, `inv_clean_render` and
# `inv_controls_screen`: it replaces the 1995 game this script plays; see inv-corrigida-*.input.)
#
# As inv-4fsacaet-win: INV starts at 26808. No key (inv-alone-lose.input):
# the fourth bomb hit ends it at 39083 in both versions.
28000 dump inv
39500 result lost -2000
39500 expect 4fmarte
39500 state
+0 wait 4fbar 10000
+0 state
+0 dump bar
